WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.000
Here's what those checks returned for
four DDI products on October 22, 2026.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.050
It's a snapshot, not a ranking,
so confirm on the day you decide.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.467
Only Infoblox Government Cloud has
a FedRAMP listing, at Moderate,

4
00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:18.000
and it covers the SaaS, not
the on-premises appliances.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.125
The others run inside the
agency's own boundary.

6
00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:24.013
Only Infoblox has vendor-specific STIGs.

7
00:00:24.013 --> 00:00:27.876
Only BlueCat holds an active
FIPS 140-3 certificate,

8
00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:32.549
while Infoblox's newer modules
are still in NIST's review queue.

9
00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:36.084
None of the four has a
current NIAP certification,

10
00:00:36.084 --> 00:00:38.412
and none is on the latest CDM list.

11
00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:40.992
So every candidate has a gap to close,

12
00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:44.688
in the contract or in a plan
of action and milestones.

13
00:00:44.688 --> 00:00:45.940
Now, who runs it.
